### 4. Inventario de Foreign Keys (Consistencia Multiempresa)

Esta consulta revisa todas las llaves foráneas que apuntan o salen de `companies` y `profiles` para confirmar que las relaciones de la Fase 3 son correctas.

```sql
SELECT
    tc.table_name AS table_name,
    kcu.column_name AS column_name,
    ccu.table_name AS foreign_table_name,
    ccu.column_name AS foreign_column_name,
    rc.update_rule AS on_update,
    rc.delete_rule AS on_delete
FROM 
    information_schema.table_constraints AS tc 
JOIN information_schema.key_column_usage AS kcu
    ON tc.constraint_name = kcu.constraint_name
    AND tc.table_schema = kcu.table_schema
JOIN information_schema.constraint_column_usage AS ccu
    ON ccu.constraint_name = tc.constraint_name
    AND ccu.table_schema = tc.table_schema
JOIN information_schema.referential_constraints AS rc
    ON tc.constraint_name = rc.constraint_name
WHERE 
    tc.constraint_type = 'FOREIGN KEY'
    AND tc.table_schema = 'public'
    AND (ccu.table_name IN ('companies', 'profiles') OR tc.table_name IN ('companies', 'profiles'))
ORDER BY 
    foreign_table_name, table_name;
```

